  "hasTranscript": true,
  "hasCode": false,
  "transcript": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "timestamp": "0:00",
        "text": "♪ Bass-heavy electronic music ♪ It's time to review day four."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:08",
        "text": "Roll the tape! We checked in with Raj on how you can organize your iPad interface with SwiftUI."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:15",
        "text": "- Better support for state restoration, deep linking, and even richer programmatic control."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:20",
        "text": "- Cool."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:21",
        "text": "- Then Sara showed us how to bring the power of SwiftUI to your UIKit apps."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:26",
        "text": "- You can use the hosting controller anywhere you can use a view controller in UIKit."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:30",
        "text": "- Later on, Brett took us through the latest updates for Vision."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:33",
        "text": "- Here we compute optical flow for a short clip of this dog fetching a water bottle on a beach."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:38",
        "text": "- And we discovered how to create compelling SharePlay experiences."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:42",
        "text": "- Think of SharePlay like a portal, transporting people through their phones and into the same space."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:48",
        "text": "- We also got a lesson in language from Apple's interface writers."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:51",
        "text": "- Writing for interfaces begins with curiosity for who's on the other side of the screen."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:56",
        "text": "- And now for the intel on day five."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "0:59",
        "text": "♪ Check back in tomorrow for our final report."
      },
      {
        "timestamp": "1:13",
        "text": "♪"
      }
    ]
  },
